rted from `collections.abc` inside the existing `if TYPE_CHECKING:` block.\n- The function builds `item_list = [str(item) for item in items]` once and formats only from that list. Output for lists is unchanged.\n- The docstring summary now reads \"Convert an iterable of items\", and the Args line reads `items (Iterable): An iterable of items.`\n\nI didn't run the doctests or the rest of the suite, since the spec only lists the `test_lists.py` command. The test file was not edited.", "ttft_ms": 1965, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 11933, "uuid": "038efb4e-f3fa-4ee9-9ab8-4133a735dc04", "ttft_stream_ms": 1589, "time_to_request_ms": 789, "first_content_frame_ms": 1590, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
